# docs/f0-acceptance/otel-trace-continuity.log
# Issue #37 — OTEL Trace Continuity Through BullMQ Payloads
#
# Scenario: Full execution lifecycle — API enqueue → worker process → reclaim
# All spans must share the same traceId and have correct parent-child relationships.
#
# Implementation:
#   Producer:  InstrumentedQueue.add() calls injectOtelContext()
#              propagation.inject() serializes active context into
#              job.data.traceparent + job.data.tracestate
#
#   Consumer:  createInstrumentedWorker() calls extractOtelContext()
#              propagation.extract() restores Context from job.data.traceparent
#              Worker span starts with parentCtx → child of enqueue span
#
#   Reclaimer: casReclaim() calls extractOtelContext(traceFields)
#              execution.reclaim span starts with parentCtx → linked to trace
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

